\code{paint_data_frame()} draws on the current base graphics device.
\code{gpaint_data_frame()} returns a \code{ggplot} object. \code{paint_df()} and \code{gpaint_df()}
are aliases.

Each column is its own formatting unit, because a data frame's columns are
independent variables: a \code{1e15} in one column will not flip another column into
scientific notation. (A matrix is the opposite -- one unit for the whole thing,
so that the same value looks identical in every cell.)
